          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 142396,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "Thanks @85956. I'm looking at the 'Green Loans' leaflet now. The information is good, but the language is a bit technical. For example, instead of 'leveraging tax-efficient wrappers for portfolio growth', maybe we can say 'grow your savings while helping the planet'. We need to keep the language simple and accessible for a general audience.",
            "mentions": [
              85956
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 142396,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "Also, there's a sentence that says 'this investment guarantees a positive return'. We need to be very careful with wording like that. According to A3, we can't make guarantees about performance. It should be rephrased to mention potential returns and associated risks.",
            "mentions": [
              85956
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A3"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "warning",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 85956,
            "reply_to": "M40",
            "text": "But it's a very safe fund. I thought it was ok to say that. I can change it if it's a problem.",
            "mentions": [
              142396
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 30806,
            "reply_to": "M38",
            "text": "The content looks informative. For the mail-based invitations (T11), we should include a very clear, single call-to-action, like 'Scan this QR code to see the full week's schedule!'. It keeps the postcard clean and drives traffic to the online schedule.",
